WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.850
Your agents. Your repos. Your data. Your infrastructure.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.850
Otto: every coding agent, one native Mac app.

3
00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:10.850
Home shows live sessions, dashboards, usage and findings.

4
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.850
Light, dark and right-to-left, one design system.

5
00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:17.850
Press ⌘K, type or speak. Otto runs it or answers.

6
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.850
⌥Space calls the bar from anywhere on your Mac.

7
00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:27.850
Agents is one workspace: your sessions in an inbox beside the canvas, status in words.

8
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:33.850
Switch a session between Terminal and Chat, tile it with the rest, or broadcast one prompt to many.

9
00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:40.850
Threads run every structured agent: Claude, Codex, Antigravity, OpenCode, pi, Gemini, Grok and Muse.

10
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:47.850
Plans, commands and diffs stream live. Approve inline, or compare models side by side.

11
00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:49.850
Workflows opens on Runs: what needs you, what is running and what just finished, in words.

12
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.850
A run page lists every step in order. A review fans out to twelve named reviewers, each with its own conversation.

13
00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:58.850
A failed run leads with the step's own error and Retry step, on your Mac or your phone.

14
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:00.850
Pick each step’s model and effort, as in Threads.

15
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:04.350
A goal is a workflow too: it works until every criterion is checked and met.

16
00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:05.850
Optimize drafts a faster version; you apply it.

17
00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:09.850
A personal agent's Chat is a thread on the same runtime, with its tools and routines.

18
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.850
Scheduled tasks run agents on a cadence and report back.

19
00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:15.850
The IDE keeps your projects in the order you added them, and brings back every tab after a restart.

20
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.850
Type with the language server beside you, run a test configuration and see the results.

21
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.850
Debug with breakpoints, frames and variables, or ask the agent about the selected code.

22
00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:27.850
Ask an agent to debug with Otto. Before anything runs, you see exactly what it will start.

23
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:31.850
Its breakpoints are marked as its own. At every stop it says what the values show, and waits.

24
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:35.850
Press Proceed to let it go on, or use the debugger yourself to take over.

25
00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:39.850
DB Watch shows the rows your code wrote at every stop: changed cells only, before → after.

26
00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:43.850
Git opens on History. Your uncommitted changes are its top row.

27
00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:47.850
Stage, commit and draft the message there. Multi-agent review turns findings into tracked fixes.

28
00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:51.850
A story's Design tab lists the designs that implement it.

29
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:55.850
Design Hall is the one home for designs: versions, compare, approve, and comments pinned on the design.

30
00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:59.850
The Vault links your docs with backlinks. Skills Lab is the one home for agent skills.

31
00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:03.850
Query MySQL, Postgres, MongoDB, Redis and ClickHouse.

32
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:07.850
A read-only connection refuses writes. History spans every connection.

33
00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:11.850
SSH, AWS, Kubernetes, APIs and the web.

34
00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:15.850
An MCP server that runs through Otto can be available in every workspace, with one set of credentials.

35
00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:19.850
Insights turns your activity into key findings.

36
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:23.850
Usage shows what is left on each plan, per login.

37
00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:26.850
Start a room from a live session. The host admits who joins.

38
00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.850
Share a screen and talk it through.

39
00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.850
Teammates draw on the shared screen, with permission.

40
00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.850
Hand over terminal control, and take it back at any time.

41
00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:39.850
With everyone's consent, get a local recap: decisions and action items.

42
00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:43.850
Continue on phone: scan, approve the match on your Mac, and the thread opens.

43
00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:47.850
Or switch the phone to the light version: five tabs, one tap back.

44
00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:51.850
Check for Updates… shows what is new and downloads the new version.

45
00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:55.850
Restart to finish: Otto lists what keeps running first.

46
00:02:56.250 --> 00:03:01.850
Snip the screen, bridge Slack and Telegram, and take Otto with you.

47
00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:07.850
Otto. All your agents, one home.
